      passage: `Both the Prescriptivists and the Descriptivists agreed that grammar instruction was important. The Prescriptivists taught rules as objective truths; the Descriptivists taught rules as historical conventions. [Therefore], neither side advocated for eliminating grammar instruction altogether — they disagreed only about its philosophical basis.`,
