      passage: `The Descriptivist movement began, paradoxically, as a defense of the Keep's original mission. The founding scholars, the Descriptivists argued, had studied language as it was actually used — not as they wished it to be. The prescriptive tradition had distorted this by elevating certain usages to the status of universal law. [Indeed], the Descriptivists did not want to tear down grammar instruction; they wanted to return it to its empirical roots.`,
