      passage: `Grammar Keep's reputation for intellectual rigor did not develop by accident. The founding scholars designed every aspect of the curriculum to challenge students to the edge of their abilities. Apprentices were given problems that no previous scholar had solved and were expected to make progress. Senior Wardens were required to publish new scholarship every three years or lose their positions. [In short], the culture of constant challenge was built into the Keep's institutional structure from the very beginning.`,
