      passage: `The Grammar Council's emergency response to the Comma Plague was widely praised for its speed. [______], critics later argued that the rushed distribution of Holt's guide created new inconsistencies — districts that received the guide at different times implemented comma rules differently, creating a second wave of confusion that took years to resolve.`,
