      pre_narrative: `The final guardian of Chapter 17 rises from the ruin floor: the Transition Tyrant, most powerful of the Logic Phantoms. It has constructed a passage of maximum complexity, where the correct transition requires understanding a three-step logical argument. No Scholar has defeated it by guessing.`,
      passage: `The Descriptivist scholars had a problem: their own arguments were being used against them. Every time they cited a real-world example of a so-called "incorrect" usage that was actually widely understood, the Prescriptivists countered that widespread use of an error did not make it acceptable. The Descriptivists needed a better argument than mere frequency of use. [______], they developed what they called the "communicative success" standard: if a usage reliably conveyed the intended meaning to its audience, it was, by definition, functioning correctly — regardless of what the rulebooks said.`,
